\title{Free-arity nerve and its explicit exactness obligation}
\taxon{Development}
\meta{layer}{human}
\meta{source}{Kernel/Augmented/ArityNerveComparison.lean}
\tag{foundation}
\tag{augmented}

\p{Under \ref{dec-kr-0015}, \ref{dec-kr-0018} and \ref{at-fd-0007}, \code{Nerve.Theory} is the full category of free augmented algebras on any supplied small arity functor into generating graphs. \code{baseNerve}, \code{algebraNerve}, \code{restriction} and \code{restrictionIso} construct the actual presheaf square. The arity-to-theory functor is the identity on objects; restriction reflects isomorphisms and preserves reflexive coequalizers, so \code{restrictionMonadicEquivalence} proves its monadicity. The other monadic equivalence is supplied by \ref{augmented-monadicity}.}
\p{\code{AdjunctionAlgebraImage.monadMap} constructs a comparison from lawful algebra operations over an adjunction, with its unit and multiplication laws proved. \code{arityMonadMap} applies this to operations transported along the actual restriction isomorphism. \code{arityComparisonIso} proves compatibility of the two monadic comparisons. None of these constructions assumes comparison invertibility.}
\p{\code{algebraNerve_full} and \code{algebraNerve_essImage_iff} now prove full faithfulness and recognition for this augmented nerve under two explicit hypotheses: density of the supplied arity functor, and pointwise invertibility of its canonical \code{arityMonadMap.comparison}. A presheaf is then an augmented nerve exactly when its restriction is a base nerve. Faithfulness and the necessary essential-image condition have weaker hypotheses, recorded separately.}
\p{\strong{Next arity obligation:} \ref{augmented-finite-incidence} now constructs a small dense candidate of finite incidence diagrams. Prove invertibility of this specific comparison for that candidate, or supply and verify another arity presentation. A presentation must retain ordered paths, every shared side, nullary inputs, empty outputs and \code{(0,0)} cells. The elementary representables are dense in the base, but have not been proved to satisfy the monad arity condition. Finite raw-term leaves alone do not prove filtered-colimit preservation. A row serialization alone supplies neither a canonical diagram category nor normalization or factorization.}
\p{The full BMW arity-to-exactness theorem and the augmented arity application are still open. After those shape obligations, the labelled diagram model must supply the cofibrant sources, relative restriction and replacement lemmas required by the existing AT-FD-7 statement, using Reedy/elegance if proved or a concrete alternative. These partial results do not pass or weaken \ref{at-kr-0002}, \ref{at-kr-0008} or AT-FD-7. Cites: \ref{dec-rt-0030}, \ref{dec-wf-0008}, \ref{dec-wf-0010}.}

\p{\strong{Finite incidence candidate:} \ref{augmented-finite-incidence} proves closure of finite generators under complete incidence, filtered reconstruction of each generating presheaf, and the equivalence between finite incidence and finite presentability. It constructs a small fully faithful dense candidate family of finite incidence diagrams and applies the conditional nerve theorem. Canonical-comparison invertibility for the generating monad remains open; no normalization or labelled diagram-model result is asserted. The full acceptance statements and statuses remain unchanged.}

\p{\strong{Finitary exactness reduction:} \code{GeneratingFiniteNerve} proves filtered-colimit preservation by the finite-incidence base nerve, factorization through finite supports, and finite-stage witnesses for equality of maps. \code{freeNerveComparison_eq} identifies the actual comparison on each arity of a fully faithful family with the representable Kan-extension isomorphism. \code{isIso_of_finiteIncidence} detects isomorphisms of filtered-colimit-preserving functors on the small finite family. Consequently, \code{finiteIncidence_exactness_iff_finitary} proves global canonical-comparison invertibility equivalent to filtered-colimit preservation by the actual generating monad. The augmented nerve theorem follows under this one remaining hypothesis; finitarity itself and the labelled diagram model remain open. Acceptance statements, versions and statuses are unchanged.}
